    {'para': '**178. Verbs. Imperfect Active, ⟨a⟩-conjugation.** The imperfect is formed from the present-stem by prefixing the augment ⟨a⟩, and adding a set of secondary endings.'},
    {'para': '**179.** If the present-stem begin with a vowel, the augment unites with it to form always the *vṛddhi*-vowel, not the *guṇa*: thus ⟨a⟩ + ⟨i⟩ or ⟨ī⟩ or ⟨e⟩ = ⟨ai⟩; ⟨a⟩ + ⟨u⟩ or ⟨ū⟩ = ⟨au⟩; ⟨a⟩ + ⟨ṛ⟩ = ⟨ār⟩.'},
    {'para': '**180.** If a preposition be prefixed, the augment comes between preposition and verb, as in Greek; thus, from ⟨upa-nī⟩, impf.-stem ⟨upānaya⟩, i. e. ⟨upa⟩ + ⟨a⟩ + ⟨naya⟩; ⟨vi-nī⟩, impf.-stem ⟨vyanaya⟩.'},
    {'para': '**181.** The inflection in the active is as follows:'},
